SUMMARY:[OOPSLA 27] R1 Submission Deadline
DESCRIPTION:Extracted automatically by a small language model\; please cro
 ss-check against the source before relying on it: https://conf.researchr.
 org/track/splash-2027/splashoopsla2027\n\nPlease submit using HotCRP: htt
 ps://oopsla27.hotcrp.com/. Initial submissions must be at most 23 pages\;
  revisions can go up to a maximum of 25 pages. PACMPL uses double-blind r
 eviewing. At least one author must be registered as a Reserve Reviewer. P
 apers rejected in Round 1 cannot be resubmitted in Round 2.\n\nSubmit at:
  https://oopsla27.hotcrp.com/\n\nhttps://github.com/JonasAlaif/pl-confere
 nces
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:4fc4cb5761cf99c70fcdb1cce97eea63bde6b327@pl-conferences
DTSTAMP:20260916T131008Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261015
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:[ESOP 27] R2 Submission Deadline
DESCRIPTION:Extracted automatically by a small language model\; please cro
 ss-check against the source before relying on it: https://etaps.org/2027/
 cfp/\n\nESOP: regular research papers of max 25 pp\, experience reports o
 f max 15 pp\, and fresh perspectives providing new insights on programmin
 g languages and systems of max 15 pp. There is no page limit at the submi
 ssion time. Please refer to https://etaps.org/2027/esop for more details.
  Submitted papers must be in English\, presenting original research. They
  must be unpublished and not submitted for publication elsewhere. In part
 icular\, simultaneous submission of the same contribution to multiple ETA
 PS conferences is forbidden. Submissions must follow the formatting guide
 lines of Springer's LNCS (use the llncs.cls class) - except for ESOP\, se
 e above - and be submitted electronically in pdf through the Easychair au
 thor interface of the respective conference. Data availability statement 
 in proceedings papers is mandatory for all ETAPS conference papers. It is
  to be placed just before the references and does not count into the page
  limit. ETAPS conferences will use double-blind reviewing (in the case of
  TACAS and iFS\, only for regular research papers). Authors are asked to 
 omit their names and institutions\; refer to prior work in the third pers
 on\, just as prior work by others\; not to include acknowledgments that m
 ight identify them. If authors do not obey the double-blind submission po
 licy or do not specify their conflicts of interest in the submission syst
 em\, this may result in a desk rejection of the paper. ESOP\, TACAS and F
 oSSaCS will use an author rebuttal phase.\n\nSubmit at: https://esop27.ho
 tcrp.com/\n\nhttps://github.com/JonasAlaif/pl-conferences
END:VEVENT
